  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 4, 'Planning and implementing a digital health enterprise: phases, steps and resources'. Seven numbered phases — assessing the current state and enabling environment; establishing a shared understanding and strategic planning; defining the future state; planning the enterprise architecture; determining health content requirements; M&E and fostering data use; and implementing, maintaining and scaling — each with its steps. Resource tiles are placed against the phases they serve and marked as PDF or online, among them the DIIG, the WHO SMART guidelines with digital adaptation kits, TOGAF, OpenHIE and the WHO handbook for health supply chain architecture. The tile 'WHO handbook for health product catalogue (this document)' is highlighted in phase 07. It is the same chart as Fig. 6 of the WHO handbook for digitalizing primary health care, re-pointed to this document.",
